WEBVTT

00:06:57.003 --> 00:07:01.073
the token right-of-center columnist
for "The New York Times,"

00:07:01.097 --> 00:07:03.713
who half the readership loved to hate,

00:07:03.737 --> 00:07:06.590
and others were dazzled by, for sure.

00:07:06.614 --> 00:07:08.615
But you were seen very much in that lens.

00:07:08.639 --> 00:07:10.407
People saw you as a Republican

00:07:10.431 --> 00:07:13.846
and were interested in these other pieces
that you brought to the table.

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:18.252
And then, there was this shift
to more talk of moral issues and meaning.

00:07:18.276 --> 00:07:20.884
And people wondered whether
this was more about you,

00:07:20.908 --> 00:07:23.782
that you yourself were going
through some kind of transition.

00:07:23.806 --> 00:07:25.534
I mean, to what extent is that true?

00:07:25.558 --> 00:07:26.717
DB: It's somewhat true.

00:07:26.741 --> 00:07:30.075
but I'm a very average person
with above-average communication skills.